values ('bbbb0003-0000-4000-8000-00000000001f', 'en', null, 'Organizational Behavior', 'Organizational behavior is the study of how people think, feel, and act inside organizations, and how to lead teams and shape workplaces that perform. This course covers the individual, group, and organizational levels, from personality and motivation to leadership, culture, and change, grounded in classic studies such as the Hawthorne research. Structure and topics are adapted from the entry on organizational behavior in Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia (CC BY-SA 4.0).', null, 'foundations', 31, true, 'business', '{}')
on conflict (id) do nothing;

